    "Proposed ru additions for src/data/claims-lint.json (patterns.ru per rule) and src/data/keyword-map.json (M3 ru, 2026-10-06). Not merged: the lead merges them.",
    "Patterns are matched case-insensitively with the u flag (claims-lint: 'ui'; keyword-map: 'iu'). Cyrillic word edges are written as (?<![\\p{L}]) / (?![\\p{L}]) and letters as \\p{L}, so the patterns behave the same with or without the Unicode-aware \\w / \\W / \\b rewrite that compileAll applies since bb689eb.",
    "claimsLint covers every rule that has per-locale patterns and no ru key yet (selection-translate and jargon already have ru; io-home and engine-claim are '*' only). ext-language-count is included although ru has no Chrome extension page (the rule is 'only: chromeExtension.').",
    "keywordMap.seOwned / seOwnedLead extend the existing ru entries (nothing is replaced); reservedG1 is new for ru. The existing seOwnedLead '^\\W*(учить|изучение) английск' was not anchored for Cyrillic headings before bb689eb (\\W matched Cyrillic letters); bb689eb fixed that. The proposed lead patterns use an explicit ^[\\s\\p{P}\\p{S}]* prefix and work either way.",
    "Tested in a fresh copy of HEAD bb689eb + ru: 0 hits on src/locales/ru.json; all 59 counter-example sentences listed in docs/redesign-2026/ops/m3/ru-qa.md (appendix A) are caught by the rule they target, also through compileAll; 5 generic language-learning phrases (e.g. «Для изучающих языки») pass."
  ],
